/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'
  Reporting-Endpoints: csp-endpoint="https://api.cireweddings.com/api/csp-report"
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src-attr 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: https://api.cireweddings.com http://localhost:8787; connect-src 'self' https://api.cireweddings.com http://localhost:8787; frame-src 'none'; worker-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; report-uri https://api.cireweddings.com/api/csp-report; report-to csp-endpoint

/claim*
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer

# Long-cache the immutable, content-hashed Astro bundles — this now includes
# the self-hosted font files the comment above describes, which used to come
# from fonts.gstatic.com with this exact header and lost it on the move to
# our own origin (xchromo/osn-tracker#131). Every path under /_astro/ carries
# a content hash in the filename, so a year-long cache is unconditionally
# safe: a changed file is a new URL, never the same one with different bytes.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Landed with the organiser's policy (VP-S-L3 said do both together — the two
# portals share a shape). Same staging: an ENFORCED line carrying only
# directives that cannot break a working page, plus a REPORT-ONLY line carrying
# the real lock-down, reporting to cire-api's first-party collector until a
# real-browser pass over sign-in, the claim link and the enquiry list comes back
# clean. Flip the header name to `Content-Security-Policy` then.
#
# GOOGLE FONTS ARE GONE from `style-src` and `font-src`, and that is a source
# change rather than a tightening on a guess: `astro.config.mjs` now downloads
# Schibsted Grotesk and Cormorant Garamond at build time via
# `fontProviders.google()`, and none of the three page shells links
# fonts.googleapis.com any more. The comment that stood here said "self-host
# here too and both entries go" — this is that. It matters most on `/claim`,
# which is opened straight from an emailed invite: that page used to tell Google
# about every vendor who followed the link, before rendering a word.
#
# `script-src 'unsafe-inline'` is now load-bearing rather than incidental: the
# theme-boot script (`THEME_BOOT_SCRIPT`) is `is:inline` on all three shells so
# it can run before first paint, and an inline script cannot be an external
# hashed file. Astro's island bootstrap is external `/_astro/*` and covered
# by 'self'.
#
# Other differences from `cire/host/public/_headers`, audited from source:
#   - No `blob:` in `img-src`: no cropper, no object URLs (`data:` is kept for
#     inline SVG data URIs).
#   - `connect-src` is cire-api only. Sign-in is a top-level redirect through
#     cire/api's OIDC leg and account management links out to musubi — both
#     navigations, which no `connect-src` governs. The localhost entry keeps a
#     local `wrangler pages dev dist` pointed at a local API.
#
# On avatars: `ProfileMenu` renders the OIDC `picture` claim, which can point at
# ANY https host — it is unvalidated at every hop between osn-api and here, so
# the sink (`AccountAvatar.httpsAvatarUrl`) is what enforces the scheme.
#
# The `img-src` above does NOT currently restrain it, and it is worth being
# precise about why, because the organiser's copy of this comment reads as
# though it does. `img-src` lives only on the REPORT-ONLY line; the enforced
# header carries `frame-ancestors`, `object-src` and `base-uri` and nothing
# else. So the allowlist is **staged, not active**: today it would only file a
# violation report, not block the request.
#
# That is fine while nothing populates the claim — osn-api writes `avatarUrl`
# null on registration and on erasure, and has no update path — but it is the
# thing to fix *before* OSN ships avatar hosting, or the portal starts issuing
# a request to a user-named host on every page load, carrying the vendor's IP
# and a `strict-origin-when-cross-origin` Referer. Bind promoting this policy to
# enforcement to that milestone, and add the avatar host here at the same time.
#
# The `/claim*` rule above only overrides `Referrer-Policy` (a claim token rides
# in the URL); Cloudflare merges the rules, so that path keeps both CSP headers.
